  "summary": "Wooden Mask of Kushmandi, also known as Kushmandi Mask or Gomira Dance  Mask and locally as Mukha, is a traditional cultural heritage of Kushmandi, Dakshin Dinajpur in the Indian state of West Bengal.",
  "description": "Wooden Mask of Kushmandi, also known as Kushmandi Mask or Gomira Dance  Mask and locally as Mukha, is a traditional cultural heritage of Kushmandi, Dakshin Dinajpur in the Indian state of West Bengal. It is a ritualistic non-vocal dance form mask worn by the local communities during the performance, to usher in Good forces and drive out Evil forces from the Villages.\n\nKushmandi's Wooden Mask has been accredited with a Geographical Indication (GI) tag in 2018.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, West Bengal; registration 2017–18), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
